msgstr "Étant donné que les tableaux offrent généralement de meilleures performances par rapport aux dictionnaires, il est conseillé d'effectuer tout post-traitement directement sur les objets `BitArray` plutôt que sur des dictionnaires de comptages. La classe `BitArray` offre une gamme de méthodes pour effectuer certaines opérations de post-traitement courantes :\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Result metadata {#result-metadata}"
msgstr "Métadonnées des résultats {#result-metadata}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the execution results, both the `PrimitiveResult` and `SamplerPubResult` objects contain a metadata attribute about the job that was submitted. The metadata containing information for all submitted PUBs (such as the various [runtime options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options) available) can be found in the `PrimitiveResult.metatada`, while the metadata specific to each PUB is found in `SamplerPubResult.metadata`.\n"
msgstr "En plus des résultats d'exécution, les objets `PrimitiveResult` et `SamplerPubResult` contiennent un attribut de métadonnées sur le job soumis. Les métadonnées contenant des informations pour tous les PUBs soumis (telles que les diverses [options de runtime](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options) disponibles) se trouvent dans `PrimitiveResult.metatada`, tandis que les métadonnées spécifiques à chaque PUB se trouvent dans `SamplerPubResult.metadata`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The client-side Sampler submits its workload as an [Executor](/guides/executor-input-output) job. The metadata of the underlying Executor result, which includes execution timing information called [_execution spans_](#execution-spans), is available under the `\"executor\"` key of `PrimitiveResult.metadata`.\n"
msgstr "Le Sampler côté client soumet sa charge de travail sous forme de job [Executor](/guides/executor-input-output). Les métadonnées du résultat Executor sous-jacent, qui comprennent des informations temporelles d'exécution appelées [_execution spans_](#execution-spans), sont disponibles sous la clé `\"executor\"` de `PrimitiveResult.metadata`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"In the metadata field, primitive implementations can return any information about execution that is relevant to them, and there are no key-value pairs that are guaranteed by the base primitive. Thus, the returned metadata might be different in different primitive implementations.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Dans le champ de métadonnées, les implémentations primitives peuvent retourner toutes les informations sur l'exécution qui leur sont pertinentes, et il n'y a pas de paires clé-valeur garanties par la primitive de base. Ainsi, les métadonnées retournées peuvent être différentes dans différentes implémentations de primitives.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"execution-spans\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"execution-spans\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "View execution spans {#view-execution-spans}"
msgstr "Afficher les spans d'exécution {#view-execution-spans}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The client-side Sampler uses Executor to run jobs, which executes its work on the QPU in _chunks_. The timing of each chunk is in `result.metadata[\"executor\"].chunk_timing`, a list of [`ChunkSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-chunk-span) objects. Each `ChunkSpan` has `start` and `stop` timestamps and a list of `parts`, where each part gives an item index (`idx_item`) and the number of configurations from that item (`size`) that ran in the chunk.\n"
msgstr "Le Sampler côté client utilise Executor pour exécuter les jobs, qui exécute son travail sur le QPU par _chunks_. Le timing de chaque chunk se trouve dans `result.metadata[\"executor\"].chunk_timing`, une liste d'objets [`ChunkSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-chunk-span). Chaque `ChunkSpan` a des horodatages `start` et `stop` et une liste de `parts`, où chaque part donne un index d'élément (`idx_item`) et le nombre de configurations de cet élément (`size`) exécutées dans le chunk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampler creates one Executor program item per PUB, so `idx_item` is the index of the PUB, in the order the PUBs were given to `run()`. If twirling is enabled, each randomization of each parameter value set counts as a separate configuration.\n"
msgstr "Sampler crée un élément de programme Executor par PUB, donc `idx_item` est l'index du PUB, dans l'ordre où les PUBs ont été donnés à `run()`. Si le twirling est activé, chaque randomisation de chaque jeu de valeurs de paramètres compte comme une configuration distincte.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To visualize the timings, pass the list to [`draw_chunk_timings`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/visualization-draw-chunk-timings), as shown in the following example.\n"
msgstr "Pour visualiser les timings, passe la liste à [`draw_chunk_timings`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/visualization-draw-chunk-timings), comme dans l'exemple suivant.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To learn what the chunk timestamps mean, how to read the plot, and why gaps can appear between chunks, see [View execution spans](/guides/executor-input-output#execution-spans) in the Executor inputs and outputs guide.\n"
msgstr "Pour savoir ce que signifient les horodatages des chunks, comment lire le graphique et pourquoi des écarts peuvent apparaître entre les chunks, voir [Afficher les execution spans](/guides/executor-input-output#execution-spans) dans le guide des entrées et sorties d'Executor.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"legacy-execution-spans\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"legacy-execution-spans\"></span>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution spans in the legacy Sampler {#execution-spans-in-the-legacy-sampler}"
msgstr "Execution spans dans l'ancien Sampler {#execution-spans-in-the-legacy-sampler}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As of `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, the legacy server-side Sampler is deprecated. The client-side Sampler does not return `ExecutionSpans` objects; use the [chunk timing](#execution-spans) described previously instead. See [Migrate to client-side primitives](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) for instructions to migrate.\n"
msgstr "À partir de `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, l'ancien Sampler côté serveur est obsolète. Le Sampler côté client ne retourne pas d'objets `ExecutionSpans` ; utilise plutôt le [timing des chunks](#execution-spans) décrit précédemment. Voir [Migrer vers les primitives côté client](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) pour les instructions de migration.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"**Click to learn more.**\">\n"
"    The results of jobs from the legacy server-side [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) contain execution timing information in `result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]`, in the form of an [`ExecutionSpans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-spans) object. This object is a list-like container of [`ExecutionSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-span) objects, each of which indicates a start time, a stop time, and a specification of which shots were collected in the span.\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"**Clique pour en savoir plus.**\">\n"
"    Les résultats des jobs de l'ancien [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) côté serveur contiennent des informations temporelles d'exécution dans `result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]`, sous la forme d'un objet [`ExecutionSpans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-spans). Cet objet est un conteneur de type liste d'objets [`ExecutionSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-span), chacun indiquant une heure de début, une heure de fin et une spécification des shots collectés dans le span.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    An execution span specifies which data was executed during its window by providing an [`ExecutionSpan.mask`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-span#mask) method. This method, given any PUB index, returns a boolean mask that is `True` for all shots executed during its window. If, for example, a PUB has shape `(2, 3)` and was run with four shots, then the mask's shape is `(2, 3, 4)`. See the [execution_span](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span) API page for full details.\n"
msgstr "    Un execution span spécifie quelles données ont été exécutées pendant sa fenêtre en fournissant une méthode [`ExecutionSpan.mask`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-span#mask). Cette méthode, étant donné n'importe quel index de PUB, retourne un masque booléen qui est `True` pour tous les shots exécutés pendant sa fenêtre. Si, par exemple, un PUB a la forme `(2, 3)` et a été exécuté avec quatre shots, alors la forme du masque est `(2, 3, 4)`. Voir la page API [execution_span](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span) pour tous les détails.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python noexec\n"
"    from qiskit.primitives import BitArray\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    spans = result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]\n"
msgstr "    spans = result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Get the mask of the 1st PUB for the 0th span.\n"
"    mask = spans[0].mask(0)\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Obtenir le masque du 1er PUB pour le span 0.\n"
"    mask = spans[0].mask(0)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Create a new bit array containing only the PUB-0 data collected during this span.\n"
"    bits = result[0].data.meas\n"
"    filtered_data = BitArray(bits.array[mask], bits.num_bits)\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Créer un nouveau tableau de bits contenant uniquement les données du PUB 0 collectées pendant ce span.\n"
"    bits = result[0].data.meas\n"
"    filtered_data = BitArray(bits.array[mask], bits.num_bits)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Take the subset of spans that reference data in PUBs 0 or 2\n"
"    spans.filter_by_pub([0, 2])\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Prendre le sous-ensemble de spans qui référencent des données des PUBs 0 ou 2\n"
"    spans.filter_by_pub([0, 2])\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # View global information about the collection of execution spans\n"
"    print(\"Number of execution spans:\", len(spans))\n"
"    print(\"  Start of the first span:\", spans.start)\n"
"    print(\"     End of the last span:\", spans.stop)\n"
"    print(\"       Total duration (s):\", spans.duration)\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Afficher les informations globales sur la collection d'execution spans\n"
"    print(\"Number of execution spans:\", len(spans))\n"
"    print(\"  Start of the first span:\", spans.start)\n"
"    print(\"     End of the last span:\", spans.stop)\n"
"    print(\"       Total duration (s):\", spans.duration)\n"
"    ```\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    To visualize legacy execution spans, use the [`draw_execution_spans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/visualization-draw-execution-spans) function.\n"
msgstr "    Pour visualiser les anciens execution spans, utilise la fonction [`draw_execution_spans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/visualization-draw-execution-spans).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    It is possible for time windows specified by distinct execution spans to overlap. This is not because a QPU was performing multiple executions simultaneously, but is instead an artifact of certain classical processing that might happen concurrently with quantum execution. The guarantee is that the referenced data definitely occurred in the reported execution span, but not necessarily that the limits of the time window are as tight as possible.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"    Il est possible que les fenêtres temporelles spécifiées par des spans d'exécution distincts se chevauchent. Ce n'est pas parce qu'un QPU effectuait plusieurs exécutions simultanément, mais c'est plutôt un artefact de certains traitements classiques qui peuvent se produire en parallèle de l'exécution quantique. La garantie est que les données référencées se sont bien produites dans le span d'exécution signalé, mais pas nécessairement que les limites de la fenêtre temporelle sont aussi serrées que possible.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
